ect short static path is not apparent. Static connectivity and the presence of a highly active intermediary (e.g. node 1132 in the top activity list, step_07, and the large khop subgraph, step_02) could in principle enable an indirect cascade, but the tools used do not provide the precise timestamps of intermediary events needed to verify a time-respecting chain. Therefore the temporal evidence available is insufficient to conclude the presence or absence of a genuine cascade.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 24564, "total_output_tokens": 4250, "total_tokens": 28814, "total_latency_ms": 63936, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}